-- title:
--   Integrality of the level inclusion x1x0LevelInclBar
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, given as a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra, let $N, N'$ be natural numbers, both nonzero, let $t$ be a natural number, and suppose $N t \mid N'$. Inside the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ consider the two intermediate fields $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by $q$-expansions, namely `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ N (N * t)`, the $q$-expansion function field attached to $\Gamma_1(N) \cap \Gamma_0(Nt)$, and `x1FunctionField N'`, that attached to $\Gamma_1(N')$; each is transported to an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ by `laurentBaseChange`, which adjoins to $L$ the image of the given field under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$. Since $Nt \mid N'$, the first base-changed field is contained in the second, and `x1x0LevelInclBar L t h` is the resulting inclusion, an $L$-algebra homomorphism $$\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L\,(\mathrm{x1x0FunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,N\,(Nt)) \longrightarrow \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L\,(\mathrm{x1FunctionField}\,N').$$ The assertion is that the underlying ring homomorphism is integral: every element of the target satisfies a monic polynomial with coefficients in the image of the source.
--
--   This is the integrality statement for the pull-back of functions along the degeneracy map $X_1(N') \to X(\Gamma_1(N) \cap \Gamma_0(Nt))$ of modular curves, in the function-field model used throughout. It supplies the integrality hypothesis needed to define pull-back of divisors and of degree-zero divisor classes along this inclusion, and is used in the comparison of the composite of push-forward along the level inclusion with pull-back along the level substitution with a multiple of the Hecke operator on $J_1$.
